1
00:00:00,722 --> 00:00:03,562
"How does a quantum computer
factor large numbers?"

2
00:00:03,725 --> 00:00:04,765
[BUZZER SOUNDS]

3
00:00:04,934 --> 00:00:06,514
- PMS?
- Shor's algorithm.

4
00:00:06,686 --> 00:00:07,726
GABLEHAUSER:
Correct.

5
00:00:11,733 --> 00:00:15,073
Four-point-one-eight-five-five times 10
to the seventh ergs per calorie.

6
00:00:15,236 --> 00:00:17,156
Prévost's theory of exchanges.

7
00:00:17,363 --> 00:00:19,653
Lambda equals one over pi-R-squared N.

8
00:00:19,824 --> 00:00:21,704
Seven hundred and sixty degrees Celsius.

9
00:00:21,868 --> 00:00:24,958
(Howard:)The approximate temperature
of the young lady in the front row.

10
00:00:25,997 --> 00:00:27,957
(Gablehouser:)Mr. Wolowitz,
this is your second warning.

11
00:00:29,709 --> 00:00:30,999
(Sheldon:)A sigma particle.

12
00:00:31,169 --> 00:00:34,589
(Leslie:)Yes, assuming the hypothetical planet
has a mass greater than the Earth.

13
00:00:34,756 --> 00:00:36,386
GABLEHAUSER:
Correct.

14
00:00:41,012 --> 00:00:44,932
(Gablehouser:)Ladies and gentlemen,
I hold in my hand the final question.

15
00:00:45,975 --> 00:00:52,355
